---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import registry from '../../generated/registry.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const generated = new Date(registry.generated as string).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<Base title="Changelog — Vermont School Budgets">
  <h1>Changelog</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every change to this site's data, formulas and citations is a commit. This page renders
    them, so the history of what changed and when is public rather than something you have to
    take on trust.
  </p>

  <div class="notice">
    <strong>Not yet populated</strong>
    <p>
      This page is generated from the repository's commit history — registry syncs, parameter
      file releases and data corrections. It fills in as those happen. The site was built on
      {generated}; there is no history to render yet beyond its construction.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What will appear here</h2>

  <h3>Registry syncs</h3>
  <p>
    The nightly sync compares the Agency of Education's directory against our registry and opens
    a pull request whenever it differs — never merging automatically, so every structural change
    in Vermont education gets a human reading and a commit message explaining it. As a
    side-effect, that record becomes a public changelog of district reorganization, which is
    something nobody else is currently publishing.
  </p>

  <h3>Parameter releases</h3>
  <p>
    Each time a statutory value is verified against current law, or the Legislature changes one,
    a new parameter file is released and appears here with its citations. The consultant
    recommendations on special education, sparsity, secondary and career-technical weights will
    arrive as a new file rather than an edit to an existing one, so the before and after both stay
    inspectable.
  </p>

  <h3>Corrections</h3>
  <p>
    When a figure here turns out to be wrong, the correction is a commit like any other and it
    appears on this page. That is deliberate. A site that quietly edits its mistakes is asking
    for more trust than one that leaves the record of them visible, and it deserves less.
  </p>

  <p>
    See also the <a href={`${base}/methodology/`}>methodology</a>, which states the current
    verification status of every parameter.
  </p>
</Base>
